(7740201, 1276535, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ErinKirsten:</b></div><hr/><i> <img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=27608" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">wolf</a> and <img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=67145" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">roz</a> I agree on the bird and appreciate the feedback as it validates my gut; I was on the fence even entering this.  Literally was checking the box and added that bird after the faint birds I had flying I didn''t think would bring it together.  I tried it in darker brown but it was too attention grabbing and since I really didn''t want it there anyway, I went for the more faint color.  I probably should have lightened it even more or left it off entirely but it was moment before the deadline and I just left it thinking that it wouldn''t do well anyway. If I were to redo this entry I would have enlarged the flying birds ever so slightly and left it at that. . . </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>"left it because you didnt think it would do well anyway"  .. !! .. ;)<br/>i had to laugh .. as this was an absolute fav in the challenge for me .. along with Anita''s with her indomitable style .. lol .. <br/> <br/>and i totally know the feeling .. should i .. or shouldnt i .. trying this and trying that .. and then sometimes even more confused .. second guessing .. what i even like and then what the voters would like .. aghhhh .. <br/> <br/>a couple things i do if i''ve got time is .. go away for a while .. and come back with fresh eyes .. thats often when i get that gut feeling ... i think than when we''re so immersed the gut feeling is smothered by the noise of our minds .. <br/>also i often duplicate the image in photoshop .. so i have one edit and another edit .. and put them side by side and go backwards and forwards looking at them one after the other .. if that makes sense .. then after i''ve put it in dpc i''ll see more things that need a tweak .. that sometimes happens many times .. <br/> <br/>the thing is .. when i think about it . those tweaks probably make very little difference to the voters or anyone who views it .. as sometimes they are so subtle .. but it has to satisfy me .. that''s when i''m invested in a pic i''m entering in a challenge .. i''m invested in very different degrees though .. some a lot .. and some very little .. <br/> <br/>anyway .. this is stunning no matter what ... <br/> <br/>and like i said .. i usually dont like saying what doesnt appeal to me when commenting on a photo .. because when it all boils down .. its only my opinion .. and you know what they say about opinions .. i wont spell it out here as it involves assholes .. please excuse the english .. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by ErinKirsten:  wolf and  roz I agree on the bird and appreciate the feedback as it validates my gut; I was on the fence even entering this.  Literally was checking the box and added that bird after the faint birds I had flying I didn''t think would bring it together.  I tried it in darker brown but it was too attention grabbing and since I really didn''t want it there anyway, I went for the more faint color.  I probably should have lightened it even more or left it off entirely but it was moment before the deadline and I just left it thinking that it wouldn''t do well anyway. If I were to redo this entry I would have enlarged the flying birds ever so slightly and left it at that. . .   "left it because you didnt think it would do well anyway"  .. !! .. ;)i had to laugh .. as this was an absolute fav in the challenge for me .. along with Anita''s with her indomitable style .. lol ..  and i totally know the feeling .. should i .. or shouldnt i .. trying this and trying that .. and then sometimes even more confused .. second guessing .. what i even like and then what the voters would like .. aghhhh ..  a couple things i do if i''ve got time is .. go away for a while .. and come back with fresh eyes .. thats often when i get that gut feeling ... i think than when we''re so immersed the gut feeling is smothered by the noise of our minds .. also i often duplicate the image in photoshop .. so i have one edit and another edit .. and put them side by side and go backwards and forwards looking at them one after the other .. if that makes sense .. then after i''ve put it in dpc i''ll see more things that need a tweak .. that sometimes happens many times ..  the thing is .. when i think about it . those tweaks probably make very little difference to the voters or anyone who views it .. as sometimes they are so subtle .. but it has to satisfy me .. that''s when i''m invested in a pic i''m entering in a challenge .. i''m invested in very different degrees though .. some a lot .. and some very little ..  anyway .. this is stunning no matter what ...  and like i said .. i usually dont like saying what doesnt appeal to me when commenting on a photo .. because when it all boils down .. its only my opinion .. and you know what they say about opinions .. i wont spell it out here as it involves assholes .. please excuse the english .. :)', '2023-03-15 23:04:34.000000', NULL, 0),
